  "claims": [
    "Pure tensor exchanges of arbitrary finite proof tracks, including formal inverses, are constructed from the existing separated one-step generator family and groupoid laws.",
    "The constructed exchange has exactly n*m local generator uses for tracks with n and m rewrite leaves. This is not an encoded size or runtime bound.",
    "Tensor path composition and inverse compatibility, synchronous diagonal splitting, and eta-template trimming are derived, without adding any higher generator.",
    "Two parallel proof tracks into a product are comparable in the existing old pure higher presentation iff both projected proof-track pairs are comparable there. reflect returns an actual higher witness from the two projected witnesses.",
    "Every pair of parallel tracks into the terminal output is comparable using right-unit naturality, unitIdentity exchange, discard naturality, and common PROOF suffix cancellation.",
    "AtomicCertificate recursively lists only atomic output proof comparisons; reconstruction and observation prove existence equivalence with comparison of the original full tracks.",
    "The number of supplied atomic slots equals the number of output atom occurrences. Every atom-free output shape has an automatically generated certificate and comparison, without assuming forward termination.",
    "The actual component-first/canonical tensor normalization obligation is reduced to these atomic comparisons. The atom-free output case is discharged for arbitrary supplied wires.",
    "The existing MAC-output counterexample has an explicit first-left atomic projection with weights 4 and 2, proving noncomparability at that atomic leaf in the OLD pure higher basis.",
    "Reconstructed tensor comparisons embed in the current mixed MAC presentation with empty support, zero old-root-definition uses, and exactly the placement requirements after contextual insertion.",
    "Given the atomic proof certificate, repaired correlated past/state/input joint-law equality follows in the updated checked MAC model."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The abstract principle of comparing product components is not claimed new. This stage constructs raw proof-path witnesses from the existing finite local forms.",
    "Atomic certificates require actual higher proof-path comparisons, not equality of output functions or individual probabilistic marginals. Product reflection must not be used to infer equality of joint distributions from matching marginals.",
    "No new local critical generator is added. The actual MAC-output atomic obstruction is not solved, and no claim of noncomparability in the richer category/mixed basis follows.",
    "General canonical tensor normalization is conditional on supplied atomic comparisons. Only atom-free output shapes are discharged without them.",
    "No finite full Cartesian/mixed homotopy basis, exhaustive root compatibility catalogue, or arbitrary atomic-output coherence is established.",
    "An atomic slot may contain a large higher witness. Neither slot count nor n*m exchange count proves proof compression, total encoded size, checker time, or fair shared-proof advantage.",
    "The correlated joint-law conclusion uses the existing endpoint soundness theorem in one updated model; it is not a new computational advantage bound or evidence of uniquely necessary higher-dimensional semantics.",
    "Code-changing computational reductions, full continuing physical execution through oracle internals and key generation, and loss/time contracts remain open.",
    "Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC work remains outside the successful full-library build. Novelty remains unconfirmed; independent review was not performed."
  ],
